IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pip-nouns`
IMPORT `pip-dates`

-- PART 7 -- PAYABILITY, regulation 32: periods of residence.
--
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Regulation 32 says what a period of residence is (in a care home, a hospital or
-- custody), on which days it begins and ends, and how separate periods are added together for the "first 28 days" of
-- regulations 30(1) and 31(1). Regulations 28 to 31 (pip-part7-payability.l4) use the aggregated days.

§ `Regulation 32: periods of residence`

-- reg 32(1): in these Regulations, a "period of residence" is a period during which C (a) meets the condition in section
-- 85(2) of the Act (care home residents); (b) meets the condition in section 86(2) of the Act (hospital in-patients); or (c)
-- is a person who is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody.
-- out of text: Welfare Reform Act 2012 ss 85(2), 86(2)
-- src:478 | 32 Periods of residence
-- src:479 | (1) In these Regulations, a “period of residence” is a period during which C –
-- src:480 | (a) meets the condition in section 85(2) of the Act (care home residents);
-- src:481 | (b) meets the condition in section 86(2) of the Act (hospital in-patients); or
-- src:482 | (c) is a person who is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody.
@ref reg 32(1) (src:479-482)
GIVEN `C meets the condition in section 85(2) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C meets the condition in section 86(2) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 32(1): C is in a period of residence` MEANS
       `C meets the condition in section 85(2) of the Act`
    OR `C meets the condition in section 86(2) of the Act`
    OR `C is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody`

-- A period of residence, by its first and last days. Regulation 32(2) and (3) say how the two days are found.
DECLARE `a period of residence` HAS
    `the first day of the period of residence` IS A DATE
    `the last day of the period of residence` IS A DATE

-- reg 32(2): for the purposes of section 87 of the Act and regulations 28 and 29, a period of residence (a) begins on the day
-- after the day on which C enters a care home, hospital or similar institution or commences a period of imprisonment or
-- detention in legal custody; and (b) ends on the day before the day on which C leaves a care home, hospital or similar
-- institution or on which a period of imprisonment or detention in legal custody ends.
-- src:483 | (2) Subject to paragraph (3), for the purposes of section 87 of the Act and regulations 28 and 29, a period of residence —
-- src:484 | (a) begins on the day after the day on which C enters a care home, hospital or similar institution or commences a period of imprisonment or detention in legal custody; and
-- src:485 | (b) ends on the day before the day on which C leaves a care home, hospital or similar institution or on which a period of imprisonment or detention in legal custody ends.
@ref reg 32(2)(a) (src:484)
GIVEN `the day C enters a care home, hospital or similar institution or commences a period of imprisonment or detention in legal custody` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 32(2)(a): the first day of the period of residence` MEANS
    `the day C enters a care home, hospital or similar institution or commences a period of imprisonment or detention in legal custody` PLUS 1

-- reg 32(3): where, immediately following a period of residence, C commences another period of residence for the purpose of
-- any of the sub-paragraphs of paragraph (1), the earlier period of residence is deemed to end on the day on which C leaves the
-- care home, hospital or similar institution or, as the case may be, on which the period of imprisonment or detention ends.
-- src:486 | (3) Where, immediately following a period of residence for the purpose of sub-paragraph (a), (b) or (c) of paragraph (1), C commences another period of residence for the purpose of any of those sub-paragraphs, the earlier period of residence is deemed to end on the day on which C leaves the care home, hospital or similar institution or, as the case may be, on which the period of imprisonment or detention ends.
@ref reg 32(2)(b), reg 32(3) (src:485, src:486)
GIVEN `the day C leaves a care home, hospital or similar institution or on which a period of imprisonment or detention in legal custody ends` IS A DATE
      `C commences another period of residence immediately following` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 32(2)(b) and (3): the last day of the period of residence` `the day C leaves a care home, hospital or similar institution or on which a period of imprisonment or detention in legal custody ends` `with` `C commences another period of residence immediately following` MEANS
    IF `C commences another period of residence immediately following`
    THEN `the day C leaves a care home, hospital or similar institution or on which a period of imprisonment or detention in legal custody ends`
    ELSE `the day C leaves a care home, hospital or similar institution or on which a period of imprisonment or detention in legal custody ends` MINUS 1

@ref reg 32(2), reg 32(3) (src:484-486)
GIVEN `the day C enters` IS A DATE
      `the day C leaves` IS A DATE
      `another period follows immediately` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `a period of residence`
`reg 32(2) and (3): the period of residence from entry to leaving` `the day C enters` `to` `the day C leaves` `with` `another period follows immediately` MEANS
    `a period of residence`
        WITH `the first day of the period of residence` IS `reg 32(2)(a): the first day of the period of residence` `the day C enters`
           , `the last day of the period of residence` IS `reg 32(2)(b) and (3): the last day of the period of residence` `the day C leaves` `with` `another period follows immediately`

-- The days of a period of residence, counting both ends; none if it ends before it begins.
@ref reg 32(2) (src:484-485)
GIVEN p IS A `a period of residence`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 32(2): the days of the period of residence` p MEANS
    IF (p's `the last day of the period of residence`) LESS THAN (p's `the first day of the period of residence`)
    THEN 0
    ELSE ((p's `the last day of the period of residence`) MINUS (p's `the first day of the period of residence`)) PLUS 1

-- reg 32(4)(a) and (5): two distinct periods of residence separated by an interval not exceeding 28 days (one year where both
-- are periods to which section 87 of the Act applies) are treated as a continuous period. The interval is the days between
-- the last day of the earlier period and the first day of the later one. An interval of 28 days begins the day after the
-- earlier period ends and ends the day before the later one begins.
-- src:487 | (4) Subject to paragraph (5), for the purposes of regulation 30(1) and 31(1), —
-- src:488 | (a) two or more distinct periods of residence separated by an interval not exceeding 28 days, or by two or more such intervals, are to be treated as a continuous period equal in duration to the total duration of such distinct periods and ending on the last day of the later or last such period; and
-- src:489 | (b) any period or periods to which those regulations refer are to be taken into account and aggregated with any other period referred to in those regulations.
-- src:490 | (5) Paragraph (4) is, where the periods referred to in sub-paragraph (a) of that paragraph are both or all periods to which section 87 applies, to have effect as if -
-- src:491 | (a) the words ‘subject to paragraph (5)’ and ‘regulation 30(1) and’ were omitted;
-- src:492 | (b) the reference to ‘28 days’ in sub-paragraph (a) of that paragraph read ‘one year’; and
-- src:493 | (c) the references to ‘those regulations’ in sub-paragraph (b) read ‘that regulation’ and the reference to ‘refer’ read ‘refers’.
@ref reg 32(4)(a), reg 32(5)(b) (src:488, src:492)
GIVEN `the last day of the earlier period` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the later period` IS A DATE
      `both periods are periods to which section 87 of the Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 32(4)(a) and (5): the interval between the periods does not exceed the limit` `the last day of the earlier period` `and` `the first day of the later period` `with` `both periods are periods to which section 87 of the Act applies` MEANS
    IF `both periods are periods to which section 87 of the Act applies`
    THEN `the first day of the later period` AT MOST (`add years` (`the last day of the earlier period` PLUS 1) 1)
    ELSE ((`the first day of the later period` MINUS `the last day of the earlier period`) MINUS 1) AT MOST 28

-- The days of the continuous period that ends with the last of a list of periods in date order. The list is read from the
-- first period on; `carrying` is the days of the continuous period so far, and `after` the last day of the period before.
GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF `a period of residence`
      total IS A NUMBER
      previous IS A MAYBE DATE
      s87 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 32(4)(a): the days of the continuous period ending with the last of the periods` ps `carrying` total `after` previous `with` s87 MEANS
    CONSIDER ps
    WHEN EMPTY THEN total
    WHEN p FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        `reg 32(4)(a): the days of the continuous period ending with the last of the periods` rest
            `carrying` (IF `reg 32(4)(a): this period joins the one before` previous (p's `the first day of the period of residence`) s87
                        THEN total PLUS `reg 32(2): the days of the period of residence` p
                        ELSE `reg 32(2): the days of the period of residence` p)
            `after` (JUST (p's `the last day of the period of residence`))
            `with` s87

GIVEN previous IS A MAYBE DATE
      first IS A DATE
      s87 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 32(4)(a): this period joins the one before` previous first s87 MEANS
    CONSIDER previous
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST d THEN `reg 32(4)(a) and (5): the interval between the periods does not exceed the limit` d `and` first `with` s87

-- Only the periods that have begun by the day count, and the last of them only up to the day.
GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF `a period of residence`
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF `a period of residence`
`reg 32(4): the periods up to and including the day` ps `up to` `the day` MEANS
    map (GIVEN p YIELD `a period of residence`
                           WITH `the first day of the period of residence` IS p's `the first day of the period of residence`
                              , `the last day of the period of residence` IS (IF (p's `the last day of the period of residence`) AT MOST `the day` THEN p's `the last day of the period of residence` ELSE `the day`))
        (filter (GIVEN p YIELD (p's `the first day of the period of residence`) AT MOST `the day`) ps)

GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF `a period of residence`
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 32(2): the day is in one of these periods of residence` ps `on` `the day` MEANS
    any (GIVEN p YIELD    `the day` AT LEAST (p's `the first day of the period of residence`)
                      AND `the day` AT MOST (p's `the last day of the period of residence`)) ps

-- reg 32(4): for the purposes of regulations 30(1) and 31(1), (a) two or more distinct periods of residence separated by an
-- interval not exceeding 28 days, or by two or more such intervals, are to be treated as a continuous period equal in
-- duration to the total duration of such distinct periods and ending on the last day of the later or last such period; and
-- (b) any period or periods to which those regulations refer are to be taken into account and aggregated with any other
-- period referred to in those regulations.
-- The result is the number of days of residence in the continuous period up to and including the day: NOTHING where the
-- day is in none of the periods. The periods are given in date order.
@ref reg 32(4) (src:487-489)
GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF `a period of residence`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      s87 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 32(4): the days of residence in the continuous period up to and including the day` ps `up to` `the day` `with` s87 MEANS
    IF `reg 32(2): the day is in one of these periods of residence` ps `on` `the day`
    THEN JUST (`reg 32(4)(a): the days of the continuous period ending with the last of the periods`
                   (`reg 32(4): the periods up to and including the day` ps `up to` `the day`)
                   `carrying` 0 `after` NOTHING `with` s87)
    ELSE NOTHING
